    <DataNode elementId="AT4G16130-MONOMER" textLabel="AT4G16130-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O23461" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">&lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; plants defective in expression of the &lt;i&gt;ARA1&lt;/i&gt; gene are sensitive to the exogenous application of the monosaccharide L-arabinose (L-Ara) |CITS:[DOLEZAL91]|. The defect was shown to be the result of the deleterious intracellular accumulation of free L-Ara. This accumulation was the result of a defect in L-arabinose kinase activity, preventing the incorporation of free L-Ara into polysaccharides and glycoproteins via the salvage pathway. A reduced L-Ara kinase activity was detected in mutant &lt;i&gt;ara1&lt;/i&gt; compared to wild-type &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; |CITS:[DOLEZAL91]|. At the time of this review, the enzyme has not been purified to homogeneity.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G16130-MONOMER" />
